    {
      "id": "text-0124",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1344,
      "y": 395.25,
      "width": 95.76,
      "height": 30.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp-0122"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0u",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 18349992,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 818472949,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1790726400000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The idea",
      "fontSize": 24,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The idea",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "text-0125",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1344,
      "y": 435.25,
      "width": 499.14,
      "height": 180.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp-0122"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0v",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 381424368,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 995988151,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1790726400000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "This is how an adder circuit works in hardware. Each pass:\n1. carries = (sum & carry) << 1: columns where both have\n    a 1 make a carry, which moves one column left\n2. sum = sum ^ carry: adds every column, carries ignored\n3. carry = carries: the carries get added in the next pass\nWhen carry reaches 0, sum is the answer.\ncarries comes first because it must use the OLD values of\nsum and carry, before sum is changed.",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "This is how an adder circuit works in hardware. Each pass:\n1. carries = (sum & carry) << 1: columns where both have\n    a 1 make a carry, which moves one column left\n2. sum = sum ^ carry: adds every column, carries ignored\n3. carry = carries: the carries get added in the next pass\nWhen carry reaches 0, sum is the answer.\ncarries comes first because it must use the OLD values of\nsum and carry, before sum is changed.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "rect-0127",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 1320,
      "y": 820,
      "width": 700,
      "height": 303.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#495057",
      "backgroundColor": "#f8f9fa",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp-0126"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0w",
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 654845206,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 135463581,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1790726400000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "text-0128",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1344,
      "y": 838,
      "width": 372.24,
      "height": 30.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp-0126"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0x",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 589516019,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1880881377,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1790726400000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Adding one column: XOR and AND",
      "fontSize": 24,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Adding one column: XOR and AND",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "text-0129",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1344,
      "y": 878.0,
      "width": 499.14,
      "height": 225.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp-0126"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0y",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1416863324,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 864486763,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1790726400000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "When you add one column of bits, there are two parts to\nthe answer: the bit that stays (a XOR b) and the carry\n(a AND b), which goes to the next column. A half adder\ncircuit is just these two gates.\n• XOR (^) gives the sum of every column, carries ignored.\n• AND (&) finds the columns that produce a carry, and << 1\n   moves each carry one column left, where it belongs.\n• Adding those carries can create new carries, so the loop\n   repeats: the XOR result becomes the new sum and the\n   shifted carries become the new carry.",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "When you add one column of bits, there are two parts to\nthe answer: the bit that stays (a XOR b) and the carry\n(a AND b), which goes to the next column. A half adder\ncircuit is just these two gates.\n• XOR (^) gives the sum of every column, carries ignored.\n• AND (&) finds the columns that produce a carry, and << 1\n   moves each carry one column left, where it belongs.\n• Adding those carries can create new carries, so the loop\n   repeats: the XOR result becomes the new sum and the\n   shifted carries become the new carry.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "text-0131",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 820,
      "width": 387.2,
      "height": 25.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#495057",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
